        },
        "doi:abef9f1c0d48853f3e51#label": "glmer"
      },
      "doi:c6b413ba96ba477b5dca#label": "To analyze flea beetle incidence we used generalized linear mixed effects model with a binomial distribution (logit link). Explanatory variables included varietal richness, color richness, percent cropland, and two-way interactions between percent cropland and the local-scale predictors: varietal richness and color richness. We used a nested random effects design of sampling point nested within sampling period nested within field. By including field as a random effect, we accounted for variation in field size, planting scheme, and management style."
    },
